    "line": 100,
    "category": "design",
    "severity": "low",
    "comment": "`logFailureMessage` no longer only logs: with `Strictness.FAIL` it throws a JUnitException. Renaming it (e.g. `handleFailure`) would keep the name honest at the call site, where the method is passed to `ifFailure` and reads as a pure logging callback."
